## The bug (MESITA-818)

Nothing in the repo could ever set `listing_type='partner'`. `_shared/save-place.ts` hardcodes `'web'` on create, no Edge Function or UI wrote the column, and the only `'partner'` anywhere was the local `seed.sql` row. Every production place was born `'web'` and stayed `'web'`.

The entire reward program gates on `listing_type === 'partner'`:
- `PlacePickList.tsx:148` — Rewards **New** tab renders non-partners as an inert "Soon" row
- `consumer-web-create-ticket/index.ts:79` — 409 `not_partner`
- venue pass + Mesita Check downstream

So Strana Guadalajara sat on the CONSERVATIVE strategy in admin (`plan='pro'`, rates 20/30/10/20, cap 500) and the guest still saw a locked row.


## The fix

`admin-web-set-plan` now owns both halves of one decision — entitlement *and* listing:

| plan | listing_type |
|---|---|
| `pro` / `ultra` | → `partner` |
| `free` (Drop to Zero) | → `web` (only if currently `partner`) |

`'unclaimed'` is left alone on demotion — it answers a different question ("we haven't heard from this venue"), which a plan change doesn't settle.

Strike 3 (`_shared/membership-strike-patch.ts`) demotes too. "Keep catalog listing" meant stay browsable, not keep running rewards — otherwise a forfeited membership keeps an openable ticket lane with every rate nulled.

**Prod data:** the one live place (Strana) was backfilled to `partner` so the Rewards tab works now. The EF itself deploys at merge time.

## Also in here — the place header

Pato's call: the stat trio is reputation only.

- **Google · Instagram · Mesita** (Mesita carries its own reviews). Zero reviews → em dash, not a fake `0.0`.
- The reward left the stat row entirely and lives solely as the tag-row chip, in **premium violet** (`bg-tier-premium` filled, violet-tinted outline when empty) so it can't read as one more grey tag. Swipe overlay and catalog tiles keep the pink ribbon.

The column is now fed for real: migration `20260803011500_mesita_review_aggregates` adds an AFTER trigger on `ticket_reviews` that recomputes `mesita_review_count` + the five averages for the affected project (plus a backfill). Nothing wrote those columns before — they were enricher/admin values only, so a submitted review moved nothing. Zero reviews leaves the stars NULL, not 0.0, because the CHECKs allow 0..5 and a 0.0 would read as a genuine worst score.
**Already applied** to the singleton via `supabase db push` — ledger was clean, only this migration pending. Trigger verified live + enabled.

## Also — the silent 404 bounce

Reported as "I cannot observe the place". The four place-detail routes resolve server-side and `redirect()` home when `consumer-web-get-place` 404s. Right call (no error boundary), but silent: the guest taps a place and just lands back on Home.

Dead ids are routine — favorites live in `localStorage`, so they outlive the rows they point at (an `admin-web-reset-database` run leaves every saved tile dangling). The redirect now carries `?gone=<id>`; `PlaceGoneNotice` states the reason and calls `forgetSavedPlace()` so the tile that bounced you stops existing.

